<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's Ansett details 1995/96 results.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's Ansett details 1995/96 results.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian airline Ansett Airways reported in its annual report that it had an operating loss before tax of A$18.6 million in the year to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>This compared with a profit of A$98.5 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>Ansett reported a net profit after abnormals of A$58.4 million in 1995/96 compared with A$52.6 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>Ansett reported total revenue of A$3.30 billion in 1995/96, up from A$3.13 billion a year earlier. It said its total debt to total assets ratio was 45.86 percent at the end of June compared with 52.85 percent a year earlier.  </p>
<p>Ansett, 50 percent owned by News Corp Ltd and 50 percent by Air New Zealand Ltd, carried 12.16 million passengers in 1995/96 compared with 11.83 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
